#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
===============================================================================
 NORA INTENT ANALYSIS  v2
 Turn-level conversation analytics for telecom intent classification
===============================================================================

WHAT CHANGED FROM v1, AND WHY
-----------------------------
v1 ran correctly but exposed three defects. All three are fixed here, and the
fixes are structural rather than patches.

 1. PII LEAK.  v1's name mask was greedy: given
        "Customer Name: Tyler Rachel\\nBAN: 871677900"
    it consumed "Tyler Rachel BAN" as the name, so the BAN rule never saw its
    own label and 871677900 survived into the report.
    FIX: the text is now PARSED INTO FIELDS FIRST, then each field value is
    masked independently according to what that field contains. A field value
    can no longer bleed into the next field.

 2. THE KEYWORD MODEL LEARNED THE PAPERWORK, NOT THE PROBLEM.
    v1 ranked "can / what / you / the" as the strongest indicators of `query`,
    and "name / email / today / call / back" for `rca` - those last five are
    the labels of the intake form (CALL BACK NUMBER:, EMAIL:), not telecom
    concepts. The model was detecting which template a message used.
    FIX: three layers, all derived from the corpus rather than hardcoded.
      (a) generic English stopwords are removed
      (b) any token that appears as a TEMPLATE FIELD LABEL in this corpus is
          removed automatically - so "name", "email", "call", "back", "issues"
          are excluded because the data itself shows they are form furniture
      (c) tokens above a derived document-frequency ceiling are removed

 3. CLUSTERING FOUND A DUPLICATE, NOT A TOPIC.
    v1 returned k=2 with silhouette 0.159, splitting 3,509 vs 112 where the
    small cluster was one sentence repeated 112 times.
    FIX: cluster on DEDUPLICATED text with frequency weights, cluster on the
    extracted problem statement rather than the whole form, and report three
    independent cluster-quality criteria instead of one.

PLUS: honest degeneracy guards. If the label never varies inside a
conversation, the "which rule reproduces the case label" test is arithmetic,
not a finding - and this version says so instead of printing 100%.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 X AND Y
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   X        the customer's problem statement, extracted from the user turn
   y_turn   the per-turn label
   y_global the conversation label
   Assistant turns are never X: they are NORA's answer and contain the
   conclusion. Using them as input would be target leakage.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 DESIGN RULES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   * No hardcoded column names, class names, keyword lists, cluster counts or
     thresholds. Everything is discovered; every constant that remains is
     declared in the provenance register as DERIVED, DOMAIN_FACT or REVIEW_GATE.
   * Reads the whole file. Chunked ingestion for large exports.
   * Every claim in the report has a CSV behind it.
   * Runs unchanged on the next export: schema is resolved by shape, template
     fields are discovered, vocabulary is learned.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 RUN
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn scipy matplotlib

   python nora_intent_analysis_v2.py --input intent_labels_all_flattened.csv \\
       --outdir nora_out_v2 --salt-file C:\\Users\\you\\nora_salt.txt

   Retype the double hyphens by hand; copied ones become en dashes and argparse
   will reject them.
===============================================================================
"""

